    {
      "id": "3w9ww7b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Neutralization Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m51gh68",
      "content": "Neutralization is the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9rtgm63",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "umcpjii",
      "content": "HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H₂O"
    },
    {
      "id": "8fgdyt9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2l4it8t",
      "content": "• Salts are ionic compounds formed from neutralization reactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7bgyqvj",
      "content": "• They may be acidic, basic or neutral."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bje7hgp",
      "content": "• Examples include sodium chloride, copper sulfate and ammonium chloride."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinguish clearly between water-soluble bases (alkalis) and insoluble bases for conceptual chemistry questions.",
        "Be prepared to identify color shifts of common indicators in acidic, neutral, and basic mediums.",
        "Master the pH scale definitions: pH < 7 indicates acidity, pH = 7 is neutral, and pH > 7 indicates basicity.",
        "Neutralization reactions and practical uses of salts are frequently tested in competitive exam questions."
      ],
      "id": "xaezrxt"
    },
    {
      "id": "d15c0gv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Uses of Acids, Bases and Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wnoa3hl",
      "content": "• Acids are used in batteries and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zio2it4",
      "content": "• Bases are used in soap making and cleaning agents."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "juzd8a7",
      "content": "• Salts are used in food preservation and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "id": "dvdodf0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z4fworr",
      "content": "• Acids produce hydrogen ions in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r8z56wc",
      "content": "• Bases produce hydroxide ions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "54dbira",
      "content": "• pH scale ranges from 0 to 14."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5aml71i",
      "content": "• Neutralization produces salt and water."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}